WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.430
This is Yoni.

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:05.459
He's from Honduras and sought asylum in Mexico
just days ago.

00:00:05.459 --> 00:00:12.040
Next Monday, Yoni will pick up a certificate
to prove he has begun the process.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.710
I went to the office for refugees and saw
that it's fairly straightforward.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:22.119
I've even heard that some people already had
their IDs after five days."

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:28.810
With that official ID, they can work in Mexico
while their application is being reviewed.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.480
Some companies even try to employ workers
at the office for refugees.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:39.560
While there, Yoni had two job offers.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:45.660
One of the jobs was in maintenance at Tijuana
International Airport and the other was working

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:51.250
for a restaurant chain here in Tijuana.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:55.899
Yoni doesn't have enough money to pay a smuggler
to get him into the US, but he also doesn't

00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:58.510
want to risk seeking asylum there.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:02.960
After Sunday's clashes, some - like Besy - have
decided to stay in Mexico.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:09.070
She saw the difficulty in getting across the
border and doesn't want to put her two daughters

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:12.660
at risk.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.780
We're staying here because of the current
situation and because of all the obstacles

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.729
they're putting in our way.

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:24.619
We know Mexico is a dangerous country, but
I've left Honduras and have nothing there.

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:28.890
Why would I go back?

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:34.950
But it appears only a small percentage actually
want to stay in Mexico - just 7% of the caravan

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.840
migrants have sought asylum in Mexico.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:42.829
This despite the large number of jobs the
regional government has offered, or the straightforward

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:44.270
asylum process.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:49.020
Getting into the United States remains the
migrants' ultimate goal.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.130
500 people have requested a visa on humanitarian
grounds.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.369
Considering there are seven or eight thousand
people, it's not very many.

00:01:57.369 --> 00:02:01.049
We believe that they might warm up to the
idea in the coming days, if they really are

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:07.850
escaping their home countries because they
are in danger there.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:14.260
Around 1,700 other Central American migrants
have volunarily sought repatriation to their

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.430
homelands.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:20.870
That number has tripled this week to 30 people
per day.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:27.730
Some migrants, like Jorge, felt intimidated
by the US police's stance against the migrants.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.900
The Americans aren't going to back down.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.090
They're not going to open the gates.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:33.920
What are we going to do here?

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.920
Nothing.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:39.310
It's better that we go back to our home countries
and work there...even if we can't get much

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:43.590
work, it's better than being here."

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:49.450
The American dream is, for some at least,
just that...a dream too far-fetched to realise.

